# Week 7 Maven Lab - Step by Step Commands

## 0. Install and Open Eclipse IDE

* Download Eclipse IDE from [https://www.eclipse.org/downloads/](https://www.eclipse.org/downloads/)
* Install and launch Eclipse.
* Select a workspace folder where all projects will be saved.

## 1. Install Maven Plugin (if not installed)

* In Eclipse: Help -> Eclipse Marketplace
* Search for: "Maven Integration for Eclipse"
* Click Install and follow the prompts

## 2. Create Maven Java Project

* File -> New -> Project... -> Maven -> Maven Project -> Next
* Select workspace location -> Next
* Choose archetype: `maven-archetype-quickstart` -> Next
* Set Project Metadata:

  * Group ID: com.example
  * Artifact ID: my-maven-project
  * Version: default
* Click Finish

## 3. Maven Project Structure

* `src/main/java` -> Java source code
* `src/main/resources` -> Config files
* `src/test/java` -> Unit tests
* `target/` -> Build outputs

## 4. Build and Run Maven Project

* Right-click App.java -> Run As -> Maven Clean
* Right-click App.java -> Run As -> Maven Install
* Right-click App.java -> Run As -> Maven Test
* Right-click App.java -> Run As -> Maven Build
* Enter Goals: `clean install test` -> Apply -> Run
* Run Application: Right-click App.java -> Run As -> Java Application

## 5. Add Dependency (e.g., Gson)

* Open `pom.xml`
* Add:

```xml
<dependency>
  <groupId>com.google.code.gson</groupId>
  <artifactId>gson</artifactId>
  <version>2.10</version>
</dependency>
```

* Run: `mvn clean install`

## 6. Create Maven Web Project

* File -> New -> Project... -> Maven -> Maven Project -> Next
* Choose archetype: `maven-archetype-webapp` -> Next
* Set Group ID and Artifact ID -> Finish
* Add dependencies in `pom.xml` (e.g., Servlet API)

```xml
<dependency>
  <groupId>javax.servlet</groupId>
  <artifactId>javax.servlet-api</artifactId>
  <version>4.0.1</version>
  <scope>provided</scope>
</dependency>
```

## 7. Configure Server (Tomcat)

* Window -> Show View -> Servers
* Add server -> Tomcat v9.0 -> Next
* Configure ports and server location
* Modify `tomcat-users.xml` for roles/users

## 8. Build and Run Web Project

* Right-click index.jsp -> Run As -> Maven Clean
* Run As -> Maven Install
* Run As -> Maven Test
* Run As -> Maven Build
* Enter Goals: `clean install test` -> Apply -> Run
* Run on Server -> Select Tomcat -> Finish

## 9. Configure Java Version via Compiler Plugin

* Add in `pom.xml`:

```xml
<plugin>
  <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
  <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
  <version>3.11.0</version>
  <configuration>
    <source>17</source>
    <target>17</target>
  </configuration>
</plugin>
```

* Run: `mvn package`
* Inspect JAR: `jar tf target/myapp.jar`

## 10. JUnit Testing

* Place tests in `src/test/java`
* Run: `mvn test`
* Check: `target/test-classes/` and `target/surefire-reports/`

## 11. Handle pom.xml Errors

* Fix typos or missing repositories
* Run: `mvn clean install`

## 12. Add Resource Files

* Place `config.properties` in `src/main/resources`
* Read in Java:

```java
InputStream input = getClass().getClassLoader().getResourceAsStream("config.properties");
```

* After build: Check `target/classes/`

## 13. Multi-Module Maven Project

* Create parent project with packaging `pom`
* Add submodules: core, web
* Build parent -> child1 -> child2
* Link dependencies in child2's `pom.xml`

```xml
<dependency>
  <groupId>KMIT</groupId>
  <artifactId>MultimoduleChild1</artifactId>
  <version>0.0.1-SNAPSHOT</version>
</dependency>
```

## 14. Create Executable JAR

* Add in `pom.xml`:

```xml
<build>
  <plugins>
    <plugin>
      <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
      <artifactId>maven-jar-plugin</artifactId>
      <configuration>
        <archive>
          <manifest>
            <mainClass>com.example.Main</mainClass>
          </manifest>
        </archive>
      </configuration>
    </plugin>
  </plugins>
</build>
```

* Run: `mvn package`
* Execute: `java -jar target/myapp.jar`

## 15. Build WAR File

* Maven Web Project Structure: `src/main/webapp/`, `WEB-INF/web.xml`
* Add: `<packaging>war</packaging>`
* Run: `mvn package`
* Deploy `target/mywebapp.war` on Tomcat

## 16. Install Custom JAR

* Run:

```bash
mvn install:install-file \
  -Dfile=path/to/library.jar \
  -DgroupId=com.example \
  -DartifactId=library \
  -Dversion=1.0.0 \
  -Dpackaging=jar
```

* Build project: `mvn clean install`
* Check dependency tree: `mvn dependency:tree`

## 17. Skip Tests During Build

* Command: `mvn clean install -DskipTests`

## 18. Generate Site Report

* Command: `mvn site`

## 19. Scenario-Based Commands

* Check error logs: `mvn -X clean install`
* Rerun failed tests: `mvn -rf :<module>`
* Change Java version: Update `maven-compiler-plugin`
* Convert WAR to JAR: Change `<packaging>` and configure main class
* Multi-module build: Build parent first, then children
